  "question": {
    "text": "A chain of mass $\\mathrm{M}$ is placed on a smooth table with $1 / \\mathrm{n}$ of its length $\\mathrm{L}$ hanging over the edge. The work done in pulling the hanging portion of the chain back to the surface of the table is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "O5a6h",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MgL} / \\mathrm{n}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3XaJO",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MgL} / 2 \\mathrm{n}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zakTi",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MgL} / \\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FKhhS",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MgL} / 2 \\mathrm{n}^{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{W}=$ change in $\\mathrm{PE}$ of $\\mathrm{COM}$ of hanging part\n$$\n=\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{g} \\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{2 \\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{MgL}}{2 \\mathrm{n}^{2}}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
